 "note": "Two squeezes are related when they share an identity. A squeeze named after IG II² has the numbers of its name (`IG_II2_2061b+2093b`: 2061 and 2093; fragments, copies and parts of one number share it); any other squeeze has the canonical identity of `<work>/phi_raw/exclusions.json`, the PHI exclusion manifest: for `Agora_I_*` the IG II² number of the Agora inventory concordance, for `IAS*` the Krateros record of its scan, else the first IG reference of the PHI texts its transcript matched (public squeezes: the annotation; TROGS-26: the system's unscored readings). A text match can be a formulaic parallel rather than the inscription itself, so it may relate squeezes that are not one inscription. Groups are the connected components over the public squeezes; data/related_public224.json lists those of two or more and the identities a TROGS-26 squeeze shares with a public one. ",
